      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::002::body",
        "PMC5893566::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC5893566::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Magnetic properties and constituent chemical identities influence the deformation mechanisms of these alloys.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5893566::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The investigated equiatomic quinary, quaternary, and ternary alloys are initially single-phase FCC.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5893566::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC5893566::web::001::introduction",
        "PMC5321736::web::002::body"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thermomechanical processing and constituent selection can be varied to alter microstructure and mechanical properties.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10056590::web::006::1_introduction",
        "PMC5893566::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC5893566::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed mechanism applies at room temperature and cryogenic temperatures.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::002::body",
        "PMC5893566::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nanotwins form during extensive deformation in CrCoNi and CrMnFeCoNi.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5893566::web::001::introduction",
        "PMC5321736::web::002::body"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nanotwins are nanostructured phases.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dislocation networks are structural mediators of the mechanical-property differences.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5893566::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "CrCoNi exhibits twinning-controlled deformation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::002::body"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dislocation accommodation governs the mechanical behavior.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "CrCoNi undergoes a magnetically tunable FCC-to-HCP phase transformation triggered by dislocation slip and interactions with internal boundaries.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5893566::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Magnetically frustrated Mn suppresses the FCC-HCP energy difference responsible for the distinctive transformation behavior of CrCoNi.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5893566::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "CrCoNi has greater strength, ductility, and fracture toughness than the equiatomic CrMnFeCoNi baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::002::body",
        "PMC5893566::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC5893566::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The superior properties of CrCoNi result from nanostructure formation and favorable magnetic properties.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::002::body",
        "PMC5893566::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The role of high configurational entropy in these mechanical-property differences remains unresolved.",
